      "hints": [
        "Factorise by grouping: $(2\\cos\\theta - 1)(\\sin\\theta - 1) = 0$.",
        "Solve in $[0, \\pi]$ to find $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the trigonometric equation by grouping terms:\n$$2\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta - 2\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta + 1 = 0$$\n$$2\\cos\\theta(\\sin\\theta - 1) - 1(\\sin\\theta - 1) = 0$$\n$$(2\\cos\\theta - 1)(\\sin\\theta - 1) = 0$$",
        "Set each factor to zero:\n$$2\\cos\\theta - 1 = 0 \\implies \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}$$\n$$\\sin\\theta - 1 = 0 \\implies \\sin\\theta = 1$$",
        "Find the exact solutions for $\\theta$ in the interval $0 \\le \\theta \\le \\pi$:\n$$\\text{From } \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}: \\quad \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$$\n$$\\text{From } \\sin\\theta = 1: \\quad \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\quad \\frac{\\pi}{2})$$"
      ],
